# DID YOU KNOW ... #

... that the  [LINK: (Washington DC Snowball Fight Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association]  was formed when around 2,000 people showed up to a snowball fight (pictured) organized over Facebook?

... that  [LINK: (Emily Sutton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emily_Sutton]  illustrated an abridged children's edition of  [LINK: (Shakespeare's First Folio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Folio]  with "red-cheeked gentlemen, sword-wielding warriors and ladies in striking attire"?

... that gamblers in Myanmar worship the spirit  [LINK: (Thone Myo Shin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thone_Myo_Shin]  to ensure victory in cockfights?

... that  [LINK: (John A. Jakle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_A._Jakle]  has co-authored nine books on "roadside America", including books on motels, road signs, gas stations, parking lots, and fast-food restaurants?

... that  [LINK: (Ellie Goulding) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellie_Goulding]  tied  [LINK: (Adele) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adele]  for the most UK number one albums by a British female artist when  [LINK: (Higher Than Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_Than_Heaven]  topped the charts?

... that  [LINK: (Robert Van de Graaff) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_J._Van_de_Graaff] , inventor of the  [LINK: (Van de Graaff generator) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_de_Graaff_generator] , turned to physics after injuries kept him from playing  [LINK: (football at Alabama) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football] ?

... that an unlockable vehicle in  [LINK: (Kururin Squash!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kururin_Squash!]  contains a reference to  [LINK: (Super Mario Bros.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Mario_Bros.]  by honking the horn?

... that the kingship ideology of the  [LINK: (Lozi Kingdom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lozi_Kingdom]  emphasised powerful ancestral royal spirits, believed to affect the present?

... that the Casablanca-class escort carrier  [LINK: (USS Anzio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Anzio_(CVE-57)]  once took the place of an entire fleet?

